    "status": "present",
    "value": "This is the streaming form of the duplicate-file task. The directory tree and path rules are the same as in variant 1, but a file's content is given as a list of chunks of any sizes (chunks may be empty). Two files are duplicates when the concatenation of their chunks is the same byte sequence; how the bytes are split into chunks does not matter. Return every group of two or more duplicate files, paths sorted inside a group and groups sorted by first path. A good solution reads file contents incrementally and stops reading a file as soon as it is known to be unique."
  },
